Why this license, briefly:

- Standard MIT grants the permissions above (use, copy, modify, merge,
  publish, distribute, sublicense, sell) with the copyright and permission
  notices preserved.
- The attribution clause (clause 2) is a standard, common addition to MIT for
  solo portfolio projects. It requires downstream users to keep the author's
  name and contact URLs visible in their distribution. This is not a
  restriction on commercial use; it is a requirement that the authorship be
  acknowledged. The LinkedIn URL is included deliberately: it is the identity
  link that proves who the author is.
- Stackclimb is named in the attribution because every project sits under that
  umbrella.

- This repository exists to be copied. It is licensed permissively on purpose,
  with the attribution clause as the only condition, so a downstream repo can
  adopt the workflows without a licensing question.
